# User help maintenance

LazyCodingAgent ships an in-app **User Guide** (Help menu) backed by Markdown in [`help/`](help/).

## When to update help

Update help whenever you change **user-visible** behavior, including:

- Main menu items, panels, docking, terminal, or workspace flows ([`mainunit.pas`](mainunit.pas), [`uNavigationPanel.pas`](uNavigationPanel.pas), [`uChatPanel.pas`](uChatPanel.pas))
- Chat modes (Ask / Plan / Agent), sessions, or debugging display ([`frmSettings.pas`](frmSettings.pas), [`uChatSessionHub.pas`](uChatSessionHub.pas))
- Agent loop, system prompt, or execution UX ([`uAgentEngine.pas`](uAgentEngine.pas))
- **Advertised tools** — register in [`uAgentTools.pas`](uAgentTools.pas) and document in [`help/tools-reference.md`](help/tools-reference.md); adjust mode notes in [`help/how-the-agent-works.md`](help/how-the-agent-works.md)
- Project rules location or editor ([`uAgentRules.pas`](uAgentRules.pas), [`frmWorkspaceRules.pas`](frmWorkspaceRules.pas))

## Files to touch

| Change | Update |
|--------|--------|
| New topic or rename | `help/index.json` + new/renamed `.md` |
| Search discoverability | `keywords` in `index.json` |
| Tool or mode behavior | `help/tools-reference.md`, `help/how-the-agent-works.md`, often `help/chat-and-modes.md` |

## Style

- English, concise, educational tone (this project is meant to teach how agents and tools work).
- Use markdown features supported by [`uMarkdownView.pas`](uMarkdownView.pas) (headings, lists, fenced code). No mermaid in help bodies.
- Do not duplicate the full README; the guide is for end users and learners.

## Loader

[`uHelpContent.pas`](uHelpContent.pas) loads `help/index.json` from beside the executable (post-build copy via [`scripts/copy-help.sh`](scripts/copy-help.sh)). If behavior of resolution or search changes, update this rule and README building notes.
